    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d329-a2">

                <pb facs="0576" n="536" xml:id="pg536"/>

                <head>Earl Russell to Mr.
                        Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-08-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 16, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of the 10th instant, relative to a schooner named the St. Mary’s,
                    which has been taken to Anotta bay, in the island of Jamaica, and is claimed by
                    the United States government on behalf of the owners, and I have to inform you
                    that the case of this vessel has been referred to the land officers of the
                    Crown.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your most obedient, humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RUSSELL.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
